 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "There are, but on the top of a station,\n'Twere only worth while one's own aid alone.\nHow strangely few, and very few again,\nIn towns or villages, where only\nOne man shall see another, and agree\nUpon no alterations except\nThe Time of Day. The great traveller he\nWill never know how many there himself\nAre in his journey; for all who travel\nWith other hands will come to his station,\nAnd give him another hand after.\nA boy could have been sent out again;",
